DATA NOTICE: diamond

Data files tracked by DVC in this directory (fetch with `dvc pull`):
  data.tar.bz -> ARDB.dmnd, long.fastq.gz, short.fastq.gz
  (ARDB.dmnd and short.fastq.gz are also committed to git here)

What:
  ARDB.dmnd: a DIAMOND-format protein database built from the
  Antibiotic Resistance Genes Database (ARDB). long.fastq.gz (654 MB)
  and short.fastq.gz: Illumina query reads.

Source:
  Benchmark code from https://github.com/bbuchfink/diamond. The data
  are NOT in that repository; the README here says to contact the
  author for the large dataset. ARDB: Liu B. & Pop M., "ARDB -
  Antibiotic Resistance Genes Database", Nucleic Acids Res. 2009.
  The origin of the reads (Illumina run C9V1HACXX) is undocumented.

Copyright:
  DIAMOND: Benjamin Buchfink and contributors. ARDB: University of
  Maryland. Reads: unknown.

License:
  The code is GPL-3.0 (see LICENSE in this directory, copied from
  upstream). GPL-3.0 does not cover the data: ARDB was released for
  research use without a formal license, and the reads' terms are
  unknown.

Used by:
  diamond-cuda, diamond-hip, diamond-omp, diamond-sycl

Notes:
  OPEN QUESTIONS: confirm where the reads came from and their terms;
  confirm ARDB's terms for redistribution.

This data keeps its upstream license. HeCBench's top-level BSD-3-Clause
LICENSE does not apply to it.
